---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
import { getCollection } from "astro:content";
import "../styles/global.css";
import "../styles/home.css";

const latest = (await getCollection("posts", ({ data }) => !data.draft))
  .sort((a, b) => b.data.pubDate.getTime() - a.data.pubDate.getTime())
  .slice(0, 3);
const slugFor = (id: string) => id.replace(/^\d+_/, "");
---

<Layout
  title="Gil Neto — Founder-Engineer & Senior Software Engineer, AI Products · Lisbon / EU Remote"
  description="Senior software engineer, 12 years, working on AI products. Founder-Engineer in Lisbon building agent memory and knowledge systems - capture, retrieval and evaluation - alongside B2B utilities shipped end-to-end. Open to fractional build engagements: bank-data and accounting pipelines."
>
<nav class="top" id="nav"><b>Gil Neto</b><ul><li><a href="#vault">Second brain</a></li><li><a href="#finance">Qaravel</a></li><li><a href="#experience">Experience</a></li><li><a href="#writing">Writing</a></li><li><a href="#contact">Contact</a></li></ul></nav>

<section class="hero" id="top">
  <div class="copy">
    <h1><span>The model does judgment.</span> Code does correctness.</h1>
    <p>Senior engineer, 12 years. I build AI products on that rule, infrastructure to UI: a second brain that runs my days, and finance tools where no model ever produces a number.</p>
    <div class="links"><a href="#writing">Writing</a><a href="#contact">Get in touch</a></div>
  </div>
  <div class="doors">
    <a href="#vault" style="--cc:var(--pink)"><span>Second brain</span><b>An agent that remembers, and says when it doesn't know.</b><i>→</i></a>
    <a href="#finance" style="--cc:var(--teal)"><span>Qaravel</span><b>Bank data, verified. AI explains it, never produces it.</b><i>→</i></a>
  </div>
</section>

<div class="topic">
<section class="band chapter" id="vault">
  <div class="copy" data-reveal>
    <h2>An agent that forgets is a demo. A <span>second brain</span> remembers.</h2>
    <div class="stats"><div><b data-n="951" data-stat="notes">951</b><span>notes</span></div><div><b data-n="4078" data-stat="links">4,078</b><span>links</span></div><div><b data-n="1826" data-stat="commits">1,826</b><span>commits</span></div><div><b data-n="94" data-s="%" data-stat="eval">94%</b><span>last eval</span></div></div>
  </div>
  <div class="scene" data-scene="graph"><canvas></canvas><div class="cap"></div></div>
</section>

<section class="trace-sec">
  <div class="trace-copy">
    <div class="copy" data-reveal>
      <h2>Six layers. The harness keeps the guarantees.</h2>
      <p>Mail and calendar come in. Every fact is captured the moment it's said. A nightly batch files it, rebuilds the indexes and scores itself against a fixed question set. The model judges. Code enforces.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="copy" data-reveal>
      <h2>It answers with sources, or says it doesn't know.</h2>
      <p>A daily brief, a course on anything, a draft in my voice. And when the vault doesn't hold the answer, it says so instead of guessing.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="trace" id="trace">
    <div class="stackhost"></div>
    <div class="feed"></div>
    <svg class="over" aria-hidden="true"></svg>
    <div class="note"></div>
  </div>
  <div class="cap trace-cap"></div>
</section>

<div class="topic">
<section class="band chapter" id="finance">
  <div class="copy" data-reveal>
    <h2><span>Qaravel</span> verifies bank data. AI explains the numbers. It never produces them.</h2>
  </div>
  <div class="scene" data-scene="connect" data-h="380"><canvas></canvas></div>
</section>

<section class="show" id="tools">
  <div class="show-side">
    <div class="copy" data-reveal>
      <h2>One rule across three pieces: the numbers are computed, never generated.</h2>
      <p>Bank data comes in two ways. Qocoa reads statements and ties them out. Qoriander hands verified rows to accountants. Qashew runs the same machinery for one person, and it's where the ledger and the AI boundary were proven first.</p>
    </div>
    <ol class="tools" data-reveal>
      <li style="--c:var(--blue)"><button type="button" data-tool="koa"><b>Qocoa <em>Engine</em></b><span>the trust layer</span><i></i></button><button type="button" class="hold" aria-pressed="false" aria-label="Stay on Qocoa"></button></li>
      <li style="--c:var(--pink)"><button type="button" data-tool="kelaro"><b>Qoriander <em>Closed beta</em></b><span>the accountant's surface</span><i></i></button><button type="button" class="hold" aria-pressed="false" aria-label="Stay on Qoriander"></button></li>
      <li style="--c:var(--amber)"><button type="button" data-tool="cashew"><b>Qashew <em>In development</em></b><span>the proving ground</span><i></i></button><button type="button" class="hold" aria-pressed="false" aria-label="Stay on Qashew"></button></li>
    </ol>
  </div>
  <div class="stage">
    <div class="pane" data-pane="koa"><div class="copy" data-copy="koa"></div><div class="scene" data-scene="koa" data-h="470" data-hm="680"><canvas></canvas><div class="cap"></div></div></div>
    <div class="pane" data-pane="kelaro"><div class="copy" data-copy="kelaro"></div><div class="scene" data-scene="kelaro" data-h="500" data-hm="850"><canvas></canvas><div class="cap"></div></div></div>
    <div class="pane" data-pane="cashew"><div class="copy" data-copy="cashew"></div><div class="scene" data-scene="cashew" data-h="600" data-hm="840"><canvas></canvas><div class="cap"></div></div></div>
  </div>
</section>
</div>

<div class="topic">
<section class="list" id="experience">
  <h2 data-reveal>Experience</h2>
  <div class="rows">
    <div class="row" data-reveal><span class="when">2026 — now</span><span class="what">Independent founder-engineer</span><span class="why">B2B utilities built and run solo, plus contract work on the memory layer of AI products.</span></div>
    <div class="row" data-reveal><span class="when">2021 — 2026</span><span class="what">Lead engineer <span>· Opplane</span></span><span class="why">Monolith to microservices, the LLM-integration layer, observability, a team of four to five.</span></div>
    <div class="row" data-reveal><span class="when">2020 — 2021</span><span class="what">Senior engineer <span>· Opplane</span></span><span class="why">Design system and front-end architecture across product teams.</span></div>
    <div class="row" data-reveal><span class="when">2018 — 2020</span><span class="what">Front-end lead <span>· Glartek</span></span><span class="why">The core industrial-IoT product, its component library and build pipeline.</span></div>
    <div class="row" data-reveal><span class="when">2013 — 2018</span><span class="what">Analyst, consultant <span>· Link Consulting</span></span><span class="why">Enterprise delivery, then on-site systems administration in Kuwait.</span></div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="list" id="writing">
  <h2 data-reveal>Writing <a href="/blog" class="all">All posts →</a></h2>
  <div class="rows">
    {latest.map((post) => (
      <a class="row" href={`/blog/${slugFor(post.id)}`} data-reveal>
        <span class="when">{post.data.pubDate.toLocaleDateString("en-GB", { day: "numeric", month: "short", year: "numeric" })}</span>
        <span class="what">{post.data.title}</span>
        <span class="why">{post.data.description}</span>
      </a>
    ))}
  </div>
</section>

</div>

<div class="topic">
<section class="contact" id="contact">
  <h2 data-reveal>Let's build <span>something.</span></h2>
  <p data-reveal style="max-width:52ch">Fractional build work on bank-data and accounting pipelines: the architecture, the first working version, and the handover. Remote across EU timezones, based in Lisbon.</p>
  <a class="btn" href="mailto:gilneto8.work@gmail.com" data-reveal>gilneto8.work@gmail.com</a>
</section>
</div>

<footer><span>© 2026 Gil Neto</span><span><a href="https://github.com/gilneto8" rel="noopener">GitHub</a> · <a href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/gil-neto-7b44946a" rel="noopener">LinkedIn</a> · <a href="/rss.xml">RSS</a> · <a href="/blog">Blog</a></span><span>Portuguese · English · Spanish</span></footer>
</Layout>

<script>
  import "../scripts/scenes.js";
</script>
